{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls","id":808519,"title":"[Mystery] Crystal Skulls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-14T01:46:24-08:00","id":808519,"title":"[Mystery] Crystal Skulls","content":"In <b>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</b> there is minor Artifact story hook \u2013 In Temples of Time Before archeomancers and Sleepers founds from time to time strange, crystallized human skulls like these:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Crystal_skull_british_museum_random9834672.jpg/400px-Crystal_skull_british_museum_random9834672.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Crystal_skull_in_Mus%C3%A9e_du_quai_Branly%2C_Paris.jpg/480px-Crystal_skull_in_Mus%C3%A9e_du_quai_Branly%2C_Paris.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>SotRT</b> suggests that Crystal Skulls do not having any powers beyond having inner light that can sometimes work as lamp - so often they find their final place on the desks of old seekers for Mysteries of (many) Atlantis(is). And no power beyond this.<br /> I do not like this answer to Mystery \u2013 I\u2019m very found myself of Skulls idea as myth. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal_skull\" target=\"_blank\">There is whole Wikipedia research page on Real Life found Skulls.</a> This topic is devoted for your ideas and story hooks for the Skulls powers.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Memory Library Idea</b></span></i><br /> I used them to this time as universal \u201cmemory library\u201d \u2013 (various) Atlanteans used them to storage their memories or Rotes for students to easy learn them. User of Skulls just put his hands on them and he could relive the coded memories in it as some kind of Astral scene. Still, have a problem with proper trigger to use it, beside touching it \u2013 this would mean everyone that transport them would relive the memories. Maybe some cool trigger could you advise on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T03:43:44-08:00","id":808558,"title":"","content":"Crystal skulls are a cool hook.<br /> <br /> The basis of my Mummy campaign was the drama surrounding mummified society upon discovery of one and learning it was an Uter relic of an honest to goodness Shan'iatu. That was all before <b>Book of the Deceived</b>, although I managed to use at least some of its background to retcon a little bit; certainly this was before <b>Dreams of Avarice</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T04:11:39-08:00","id":808567,"title":"","content":"I'd have the triggers vary, because Relics of the Time Before don't have to be consistent, but probably something involving demonstrating the necessary level of skill with the encoded Arcanum to learn the encoded Rote - maybe &quot;do a specific thing of the correct Practice,&quot; with &quot;specific thing&quot; varying wildly depending on where the skull was found but basically being like a codephrase.<br /> <br /> Also, keep reading Soul Cage, Dave does something interesting with these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:09:27-08:00","id":808658,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure Imperial Mysteries says they remains of Ascended and/or Archmasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:54:47-08:00","id":808694,"title":"","content":"They are (usually), but Wyrd wanted to give them powers too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:36:04-08:00","id":808730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imperial Mysteries p.73</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Sarira possesses the following properties:<ul><li><b>Divisible:</b> Sariras may be divided into pieces that often retain portions of the entire relic\u2019s power.</li> <li><i><u><b>Fragile Artifact:</b> A complete, undamaged Sarira is a 10-dot Artifact according to the rules found on pp. 80-81 of Mage: The Awakening, with the exception that it lacks the Unbreakable quality and does not store Mana as described in that section. The Tass property below overrides that standard rule. If anyone divides a Sarira into various parts, assign Artifact dot values and thematically related powers to each component. Once they\u2019ve been severed, parts of minor symbolic value retain little to no power.</u></i></li> <li><b>Tass:</b> A Sarira attracts Mana so that over time, it becomes ever more potent Tass. Upon manifestation, a Sarira collects as much Mana as the Gnosis-based maximum capacity of the mage that produced it. An undivided Sarira\u2019s Tass value increases by 1 point per decade of existence. Cutting up a Sarira divides its Tass. This does not necessarily correspond to body mass, so a sapphire that was once the mage\u2019s pineal gland might contain 20% of the Sarira\u2019s total Tass, while an entire leg possesses no more than a point or two. If it\u2019s cut to pieces, the Sarira\u2019s Tass value stops increasing over time.</li> <li>When used as Tass, the Sarira progressively crumbles or rots. This makes it impossible to recharge with Prime. When all its Mana disappears, the Sarira completely dissolves. A Sarira loses Artifact dots in proportion to any Tass expenditure, so that every 10% lost costs the Sarira an Artifact dot. If its Tass drops below 30%, the Sarira no longer functions as an Artifact.</li> <li><b>Supernal Magical Tool:</b> Whole or in parts, a Sarira acts as a dedicated magical tool to any mage with the same primary Arcana as the Ascended sorcerer, no matter their Path or order. No special ceremony is necessary. The tool doesn\u2019t necessarily possess an Intimate sympathetic connection to the caster, though it might build one over time.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>That's their powers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:50:15-08:00","id":808740,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so? Wyrd went a different route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:30:39-08:00","id":808765,"title":"","content":"Artifact of Mind spell to connect to isolated Oneiros. Done.<br /> <br /> Astral Invitation (Mind 3), plus Fate 2/Time 2/Space 2 conjuctional. Artifact 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:44:32-08:00","id":808775,"title":"","content":"You still haven't addressed the actual question in the OP.<br /> <br /> What's a cool trigger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:02:15-08:00","id":808793,"title":"","content":"Obviosly something in High Speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:00:57-08:00","id":809221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=808775#post808775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You still haven't addressed the actual question in the OP.<br /> <br /> What's a cool trigger?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'd say how easy they are to access should depend on their original purpose. Are these top secret files or just someone's personal diary?<br /> <br /> Either way, I doubt they'd design them for sleepers or even other supernaturals to easily access so they're most likely assuming that one of the Awakened will be accessing the memories. That means the easiest way is probably tying it in to Astral Travel. Meditating while looking at the skull (possibly not even requiring a Hallow or Demesne like usual) allows one of the Awakened to Astral Travel inside the artifact.<br /> <br /> If you use the whole &quot;Atlantis was a domineering imperialistic culture at war with the surrounding world&quot; theme then speaking a phrase in High Speech would be a good security measure to prevent the Tamers or the Timori from gaining access.<br /> <br /> A rote would be another good method for controlling access. Especially if it contains Atlantean secrets of one of the Orders, a very difficult rote based on their Order skills could make it difficult for other Mages to gain access even if they found the rote.<br /> <br /> If they want to keep the memories out of the hands of the unworthy, perhaps it requires some form of extended roll based on Wisdom to access. I actually quite like the idea of one of these ancient Atlantean artifacts radiating paradox when activated, requiring the Mages to channel the paradox through their own patterns and neutralizing it through a Wisdom based roll (as the Paradox is slowing tearing them apart). The artifact might even get mistaken for a Scelesti relic or misused as some sort of Paradox bomb, but the true purpose is to find a Mage with a pure enough soul to counteract the paradox and access it. <br /> <br /> At the most extreme level of difficult to access, it could require being part of an ancient Legacy with the attainments of that Legacy allowing someone access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:49:26-08:00","id":809260,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that the skulls would have originated from a time that pre-dates the Orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T18:19:29-08:00","id":809276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809260#post809260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that the skulls would have originated from a time that pre-dates the Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The Diamond Orders weren't &quot;orders&quot; back then, however they were still distinct social groups within Atlantean society. You still had the Alae Draconis, Visus Draconis, Vox Draconis and Ungula Draconis. These divisions still correspond pretty closely to present day Diamond Orders and there are several mentions in the splatbooks about old Atlantean ruins, or early diaspora ruins being dedicated to one of the particular groups more than the others.<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking 2nd Edition in which case this has been changed, however the context of the OP suggests that it's a 1st Edition based discussion, at least in my reading of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T19:45:53-08:00","id":809312,"title":"","content":"In the case of Atlantian artifacts that require a trigger to use I would expect that discovering what that trigger is would be a major mystery in itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T23:03:01-08:00","id":809392,"title":"","content":"I'd say there are several possible routes here, but I personally would prefer a trigger that is unlikely to &quot;come up&quot; by accident. Hence, the first proposal is as follows.<br /> <br /> You have to be relaxed and looking straight into the eyes of the skull, have a relevant form of mage-sight up and use Prime to activate the artifact without it's normal trigger. This pulls the casters mind into the skull, a sort of sealed off mini-oneiros in which knowledge is stored. So far so good.<br /> That feat HAS been managed more than once though; the tricky part comes next, getting out again, which requires you to know what the &quot;reverse&quot; of the above would look like (or rather inverse). This is the part that most people fail at, and eventually they die. (perhaps their minds stay in there, even when their bodies die)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T23:56:18-08:00","id":809401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809276#post809276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no. The Diamond Orders weren't &amp;quot;orders&amp;quot; back then, however they were still distinct social groups within Atlantean society. You still had the Alae Draconis, Visus Draconis, Vox Draconis and Ungula Draconis. These divisions still correspond pretty closely to present day Diamond Orders and there are several mentions in the splatbooks about old Atlantean ruins, or early diaspora ruins being dedicated to one of the particular groups more than the others.<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking 2nd Edition in which case this has been changed, however the context of the OP suggests that it's a 1st Edition based discussion, at least in my reading of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd's said more than once that his game is as close to 2e as he can get it.<br /> <br /> @2ptTakrill: A Prime Knowing spell would quickly take care of the trigger &quot;Mystery&quot; unless you started adding in more powers to it. Which it doesn't have.<br /> <br /> @Asaram: Mages are well versed in leaving the Astral. Worst case scenario they blow all their WP and get ejected.<br /> <br /> Wyrd's looking for an activation trigger, not a booby trap. Which would be another additional power. Come on people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T00:42:13-08:00","id":809414,"title":"","content":"Interesting ideas, <b>Michael</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809221#post809221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, I doubt they'd design them for sleepers or even other supernaturals to easily access so they're most likely assuming that one of the Awakened will be accessing the memories. That means the easiest way is probably tying it in to Astral Travel. Meditating while looking at the skull (possibly not even requiring a Hallow or Demesne like usual) allows one of the Awakened to Astral Travel inside the artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good and simple concept for nothing not very secret in Skull. And it would be like 1 or 2 dot Artifact they are described in <b>SotRT</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809221#post809221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use the whole &quot;Atlantis was a domineering imperialistic culture at war with the surrounding world&quot; theme then speaking a phrase in High Speech would be a good security measure to prevent the Tamers or the Timori from gaining access.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice idea for those using &quot;One Atlantis&quot;. I myself use rather there were &quot;Many Atlantis&quot;, each fitting with one another, across space-time. Still, High Speech phrase would also work in this case - each of &quot;Atlantean Empires&quot; could discover their own version of High Speech ( even if in the end it's one and the same language ) and Skull is resonating with particular High Speech &quot;dialect&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809221#post809221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A rote would be another good method for controlling access. Especially if it contains Atlantean secrets of one of the Orders, a very difficult rote based on their Order skills could make it difficult for other Mages to gain access even if they found the rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Concept usable only for those STs using Orders as coming from universal Castes of Dragon ( Wings, Eyes, Talons etc. ) - I will abstain from this, but idea on it self is interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809221#post809221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they want to keep the memories out of the hands of the unworthy, perhaps it requires some form of extended roll based on Wisdom to access. I actually quite like the idea of one of these ancient Atlantean artifacts radiating paradox when activated, requiring the Mages to channel the paradox through their own patterns and neutralizing it through a Wisdom based roll (as the Paradox is slowing tearing them apart). The artifact might even get mistaken for a Scelesti relic or misused as some sort of Paradox bomb, but the true purpose is to find a Mage with a pure enough soul to counteract the paradox and access it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the only real objection to presented concepts - Abyss <b>was not existing</b> before the Fall, whenever original cataclysm come from. But idea on &quot;Wisdom searching trigger&quot; could work for post-Fall civilizations. In the end - specific idea, but cool to use when could be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809221#post809221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the most extreme level of difficult to access, it could require being part of an ancient Legacy with the attainments of that Legacy allowing someone access.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would use it especially with Tamers or Tamori sites - spot on concept!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T00:50:29-08:00","id":809415,"title":"","content":"<b>Mrmdubois</b>, I do not need lawyer. Topic was made to talk over particular Mystery in <b>Mage </b>setting - and each mystery can have multiple answers, based on each chronicle and STs preferences. Let people talk about their ideas - even if I do not use them based on mine particular likes, maybe other STs find them interesting. Let's not limit ourselves here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809401#post809401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd's said more than once that his game is as close to 2e as he can get it.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>2ED Atlantis idea points there are multiple versions of answer to it's Mystery</b> - in one chronicle Atlantis can come from &quot;only real Empire of Magic&quot;, in other be multiple &quot;empires&quot; scattered through space-time. In one can be utopia of human potential, in others be group of fighting states between across globe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809401#post809401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd's looking for an activation trigger, not a booby trap. Which would be another additional power. Come on people.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Crystal Skull as Booby Trap could be also interesting idea</b> - not all versions of Atlantis were gracious empires. Someone you just want your millenia old enemies to be punished for looking over in to your secrets. Would gladly read more how to make those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-15-2016, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T00:56:58-08:00","id":809416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809401#post809401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd's said more than once that his game is as close to 2e as he can get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah okay. I'm still getting to know everyone here. Not quite up to the stage of matching people's names to the details of their chronicles just yet. I was thinking I was doing well remembering he speaks Polish on one of the other threads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809401#post809401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd's looking for an activation trigger, not a booby trap. Which would be another additional power. Come on people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've given three quite serious ones so far. High Speech. Astral projection. Rote. The whole paradox bomb is perhaps a little out there, but I like throwing out additional thoughts that get inspired by the conversation.<br /> <br /> If that's not enough...<br /> <br /> * Imbue the skull with your signature nimbus, then while it's still imbued rush through the astral realms to the Anima Mundi where a special new realm has opened up. If you don't reach it before your nimbus fades, the door to the memory realm is invisible to you.<br /> <br /> * Scrutinize the skull with active magesight until you attract the supernal guardian of the skull's attention and it approaches to open your mind to the memories.<br /> <br /> * Use a full unmaking effect on the skull as a sign of faith. The physical skull appears to briefly vanish while the memories flood into you. You can then relinquish the memories anytime you want to recreate the physical crystal skull.<br /> <br /> * Assemble the sacred materials of each of the supernal realms, each one fashioned in a unique supernal symbol that can be used as a Yantra. However there are only four supernal tools and five realms, the ritual doesn't work with one of the new order based Supernal implements. You have to find something far older still, the missing fifth sacred implement of the supernal realms.<br /> <br /> * Summon a being from the Supernal realm of Pandemonium as only they can access the secret lore stored within.<br /> <br /> * The activation phrase must be pronounced perfectly, but no one has mastered the high speech to that degree in over a thousand years. Maybe if you could somehow bring the skull to the realm of the Omphalos and breath in its sacred mists, but how can you bring the artifact into the astral realms and what kind of attention will that draw?<br /> <br /> * Or perhaps a great linguist with one of the language based legacies of the present world can access the skull.<br /> <br /> * Only the first person to touch the skull when it was retrieved from the tomb can access the memories in the skull, but that person was a sleeper archaeologist. Can you show a sleeper such a mighty artifact or is that blasphemy against the mysteries. Would the sleeping curse in his mind destroy the memories if he was given access to them? The link would be broken and the skull could be used by anyone again... if the sleeper was killed.<br /> <br /> * When you access the memories (which turns out to be surprisingly easy) the passage onwards is sealed by an iron barricade with the symbol of an eye upon it. The exarchs want no one to have access to this information. But perhaps a recently defected seer knows the secret of how to open the gate of barred souls, if their defection is genuine and you're not just handing the secrets of the skulls over to the greatest enemy.<br /> <br /> Any of those okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","user":"Michael Kenner","date":". 01-15-2016, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:09:15-08:00","id":809421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809415#post809415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mrmdubois</b>, I do not need lawyer. Topic was made to talk over particular Mystery in <b>Mage </b>setting - and each mystery can have multiple answers, based on each chronicle and STs preferences. Let people talk about their ideas - even if I do not use them based on mine particular likes, maybe other STs find them interesting. Let's not limit ourselves here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>2ED Atlantis idea points there are multiple versions of answer to it's Mystery</b> - in one chronicle Atlantis can come from &quot;only real Empire of Magic&quot;, in other be multiple &quot;empires&quot; scattered through space-time. In one can be utopia of human potential, in others be group of fighting states between across globe.<br /> <br /> <b>Crystal Skull as Booby Trap could be also interesting idea</b> - not all versions of Atlantis were gracious empires. Someone you just want your millenia old enemies to be punished for looking over in to your secrets. Would gladly read more how to make those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'll back off. I got annoyed with the way I was reading Tambov's tone and it just progressed from there. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:19:08-08:00","id":809427,"title":"","content":"Sorry, Mrmdubois, I was a little snappy there myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809414#post809414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the only real objection to presented concepts - Abyss <b>was not existing</b> before the Fall, whenever original cataclysm come from. But idea on &quot;Wisdom searching trigger&quot; could work for post-Fall civilizations. In the end - specific idea, but cool to use when could be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops. Yeah, good point.<br /> <br /> Although I do think that the abyss existed before the fall. It just wasn't where it is now. I think the seers found something that already existed and moved it to block the Supernal realms, rather than creating something new. I always like to imagine that The Gate was one of the very first Scelesti.<br /> <br /> However even then, it would be very strange for the abyss to be a serious concern for any pre-fall Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T02:04:48-08:00","id":809452,"title":"","content":"Cool ideas <b>Michael</b>, I will look on them in detail later and answer on them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/808519-mystery-crystal-skulls?p=809416#post809416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah okay. I'm still getting to know everyone here. Not quite up to the stage of matching people's names to the details of their chronicles just yet. I was thinking I was doing well remembering he speaks Polish on one of the other threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a Pole and running my games from Lublin in Poland for mine Polish buddies and friends. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We use Polish on game sessions, from logical reasons. But I think I should mark in mine profile from where I come - English is mine second language and even if I try to write in it as correct as I can, I know I make some mistakes. Still, most of the times I pretty understand everything what is written on those forum - well, maybe beside exotic idioms or proper names. But there is Internet for help in translation.<br /> <br /> Now I run two games - one is set in London, but is globe spanning adventure on finding secrets of Earths Chakras and confirmation if Three of PCs are Hieromagus from Guardians of Veil myths. It's <b>SotRT </b>all the way, and even my players cabal found some Crystal Skulls, in previous reality. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We play on &quot;1.5&quot; ED ( using CoD rules and Mage 2ED spoilers as much of it ) and plan to update to 2ED few weeks after new corebook comes out. More about London Consilium and setting you can read <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/21255-london-consillium\">here</a>, what are Signs of Hieromaugs in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/28578-signs-of-hieromagus\">here</a> and how Earth's Chakras are Post-Fall Archmasters Chantries <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/116909-imperial-mysteries-irises-and-chantries\">here</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I recently started also new game set in Massachusetts New England and about (Supernal) Alchemy - it is not <b>CoD</b> rulebook mortal investigators, that will become proper 2ED <b>Mage</b> when new corebook will come. More can be read New England setting to read <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-new-england-setting\">here</a> and Supernal Alchemy in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-idea-philosopher-s-stone-as-grand-mystery\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T12:46:45-08:00","id":809798,"title":"","content":"How about this: the skull is actually a form of Supernal compressed storage. In order to decompress the Astral information contained within, the skull must be pressed against the forehead of someone with no memory. The skull then dissolves as the information it stores is copied into the mind of the recipient, whose personality and memories become identical to that of the ancient individual used to make the skull in the first place. Once this occurs, the individual's Oneiros becomes the gateway to the information. As a bonus, the person becomes a Sleepwalker if they were a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> Now, is your cabal going to kidnap an amnesiac, or erase someone's memory? And what are you going to do with the Atlantean personality after you've gotten your Rotes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T13:49:12-08:00","id":809825,"title":"","content":"That sounds really cool.<br /> <br /> Time to kidnap some Hollow Ones from the Seers. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T05:09:44-08:00","id":818344,"title":"","content":"Other idea, mentioned some time before - Crystal Skulls as ancient mentors! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/288561-how-to-train-the-dragons-err-mages?p=289098#post289098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest fix in that case is to do something like use the telepath stones (or was it skulls?) from Secrets of the Ruined Temple. Basically this would give the character a &quot;bad&quot; mentor, because it would be -way- behind the times, but you're messing around with Ruins of the Time Before anyways so it ties in. On the bright side, you would have a way to teach the PC about the elemental precepts, the deer, lion and sage and to get him hooked up with the Order rote specialties and maybe even throw a few rotes in for him to learn. It's awesome, has historical value, can actually teach him what you want him to learn without soaking up lots of downtime with a mentor NPC, and when he finally does run into a Thearch they'll look at him like he's absolutely insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T23:32:17-08:00","id":1035106,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sariras-relics-of-ascension-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">Crystal Skulls being confirmed to be ex-heads of Asended beings</a> - yeah, let's collect our Atlanteans colleagues heads for their knowledge and memories! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> For this occasion - some Sariras of Atlantean mages. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/indianajones/images/5/52/Crystal_skull_(13).jpg/revision/latest?cb=20100501164151\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,